15 0 obj
<< /A 39 0 R /Alt (Flowchart illustrating the study selection process for a systematic review. Out of three hundred twenty-four records identified, one hundred sixty-three duplicates were removed, forty-five excluded at screening, and one hundred one excluded for various reasons, resulting in fifteen studies included for qualitative synthesis.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 29 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 40 0 R /Alt (Risk of bias summary table for fifteen studies, showing five domains and overall risk per study. Most domains are marked as low risk \(green plus\), with occasional yellow circles indicating some concerns, notably in D4, D5, and the overall column for a few studies. Domains evaluated are randomization, intervention deviations, missing data, outcome measurement, and selective reporting.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 31 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 41 0 R /Alt (Forest plot illustrating mean differences between treatment and control groups across multiple time points, with each study represented by a blue square and confidence interval. Diamonds summarize subgroup and overall effects, showing variability and heterogeneity statistics for each time interval. The overall pooled effect appears to show a negative mean difference, suggesting that the treatment group had lower values compared to control for most time points.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 42 0 R /Alt (Meta-analysis forest plot comparing mean differences between treatment and control groups across multiple studies at various follow-up times. Each time point displays study names, sample sizes, means, standard deviations, confidence intervals, and study weights, with squares representing individual studies and diamonds summarizing pooled effects. A vertical line at zero marks no difference, and summary statistics and heterogeneity estimates are provided for each group and overall.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
